      <title>Audi’s $89,000 Q9 Shows Chinese Competition Is Hitting the US</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-06/audi-s-89-000-q9-shows-chinese-competition-is-hitting-the-us</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">0f0a0561c7f054348b536c57</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 09:30:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>America’s automakers enjoy the refuge of an anti-Chinese wall. But so do foreign, non-Chinese automakers who also sell vehicles in America, especially if they manufacture here. This means Chinese competition is exerting pressure on US dealer lots already; indirectly, yes, but it’s likely to intensify. Detroit’s defensive moat is less impenetrable than it might seem.</description>
      <dc:creator>Liam Denning</dc:creator>
